BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Talk featuring Sally Hayden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T190000
UID:bm-6432020261026@shop.benmcnallybooks.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/7600763/Website2/
 Events/10_26_26.png?cb=1790270254
DESCRIPTION:[at Ben McNally Books]\nJoin us at Ben McNally Books for a spe
 cial evening with journalist Sally Hayden\, former winner of the Irish Boo
 k of the Year (\nMy Fourth Time\, We Drowned\n)\, and author of\nThis is A
 lso a Love Story: A Reporter's Search for Goodness in a Cruel World\n.\nSa
 lly with be joined in conversation by journalist Katie Engelhart.\nOrder 
 a copy of\nThis is Also a Love Story\nhere.\nAbout the Book\nAn acclaimed 
 reporter takes us on an unforgettable journey\, capturing the human capaci
 ty for love and connection against all odds.\nWe live in an era defined by
  crisis—whether it be war and displacement\, climate collapse\, or growi
 ng inequality\, and how the powerful profit from violence and exploitation
 . Celebrated foreign correspondent Sally Hayden has spent her career on th
 e frontlines\, uncovering some of the darkest moments of our time. Yet eve
 n in the face of unimaginable adversity\, she’s witnessed the incredible
  goodness of regular people.\nIn\nThis Is Also a Love Story\n\, Hayden ree
 xamines catastrophe through the love stories she has come across. She intr
 oduces us to a mother in northeast Nigeria who risks everything to save he
 r daughter from forced marriage to Boko Haram militants\, and to a group o
 f Syrian women who have tirelessly searched for their missing spouses and 
 children\, while launching a call for justice. We meet a couple separated 
 by the Russian invasion of Ukraine and read letters from the bereaved to t
 he dead\, still being written over a decade after the tsunami that devasta
 ted Japan. Through these stories\, which crisscross the globe\, from Ugand
 a to Lebanon\, Ghana\, Rwanda and Iraq\, she challenges us to reconsider w
 hat it means to be alive on this planet today.\nWhat if news was recounted
  through the prism of the actions and decisions people take for those they
  love? Would it become harder to dehumanize those who seem different to us
 ?\nThis Is Also a Love Story\ndares us to recognize how innate generosity 
 and self-sacrifice can be found in even the most difficult of times\, and
 —as a result—to question what might be needed to create a better world
 .\nAbout the Author\nSally Hayden is an Irish journalist focused on migrat
 ion\, conflict\, and humanitarian crises. Sally’s work has been featured
  by\nThe New York Times\, the Irish Times\, The Washington Post\, Financia
 l Times\, The Guardian\, CNN International\, Al Jazeera\, Time\, BBC\n\, a
 nd other outlets across the world. Sally’s first book\nMy Fourth Time\, 
 We Drowned\nwas the winner of the Orwell Prize and the Irish Book of the Y
 ear\, and was a finalist for the Baillie Gifford Prize and the New York Pu
 blic Library’s Helene Bernstein Book Award for excellence in journalism.
LOCATION:Ben McNally Books
URL:https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events
X-SOURCE:Ben McNally Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:October Social: Characters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T193000
UID:bm-6458020261030@shop.benmcnallybooks.com
DESCRIPTION:[Ben McNally Books Social]\nJoin us for our third social!\nThi
 s time around we'll be introducing themes to our gatherings\, and for Octo
 ber our theme will be Characters!\nAnd\, since we'll be gathering so close
  to Halloween\, we invite everyone who is brave enough to come dressed as 
 their favourite literary character! We'll have special prizes for everyone
  who comes in costume.\nCome join us to meet with fellow booklovers\, and 
 to talk to them (and us) about your favourite literary characters.\nWe'll 
 have some nibbles and some drinkies\, and we invite you to come join the f
 estivities.\nWe'll do a bit of a presentation to talk about some our own f
 avourite characters\, we'll share some news\, as well as some upcoming pla
 ns for the shop.\nBut\, more than anything\, we wanted to create a space f
 or people to mingle and socialize and get to know fellow booklovers.
LOCATION:Ben McNally Books
URL:https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events
X-SOURCE:Ben McNally Books
END:VEVENT
